-- Dialy: no organic / conventional split in the KH-Rechner. Organic and
-- conventional foods have the same carbs, so "Bio" / "Organic" is removed
-- from the food names and the translations in `names`:
--   "Bio Joghurt" -> "Joghurt", "Ahornsirup bio" -> "Ahornsirup",
--   "Gemüsereis mit Bio-Poulet" -> "Gemüsereis mit Poulet",
--   "Erdnuss-Butter stückig (Bio)" -> "Erdnuss-Butter stückig",
--   "Organic Coconut Bar" -> "Coconut Bar", "yaourt bio" -> "yaourt".
-- Brand names that contain the word stay (Biotta, Bionella, EnerBio, Jardin
-- Bio, Bio Primo, Biomilk …). Same rule as scripts/lib/organic.mjs, which the
-- Dialy-Editor applies to new foods.
--
-- Step 1 renames 608 foods (and fixes translations of 18 more). A row is only
-- touched if its name is still the listed one, so later edits in the
-- Dialy-Editor are not overwritten.
-- Step 2 hides 67 foods that are now a duplicate of an existing entry
-- with carbs within 3 g or 15 % (as in 0026), e.g. "Bio Joghurt" -> "Joghurt".
-- Nothing is deleted. The foods_touch_updated_at trigger (0010) bumps
-- updated_at, so the app picks the changes up on its next sync.

update public.foods f
set name = v.new_name,
    names = coalesce(f.names, '{}'::jsonb) || v.names::jsonb
